    fix(ci): make markdown install PEP 668-portable. Addresses QA-OFF-BY-ONE-28.
    
    The corpus-hygiene job's OB-GAP-093 redaction self-test installed the
    markdown package with a bare `pip install markdown`. On runner images with
    PEP 668 externally-managed-environment enforcement (e.g.
    catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest under act 0.2.89) that step fails before the
    self-test runs, silently removing the gate on non-GitHub runners.
    
    Chosen mechanism (option a from the task): invoke pip via
    `python3 -m pip install --break-system-packages markdown`. Minimal change,
    no new action, no vendored dependency; the flag is a no-op on images without
    PEP 668 enforcement and unblocks the install where enforcement exists. The
    self-test invocation (`make site-redaction-selftest`) is unchanged.
    
    Verified locally: `make site-redaction-selftest` passes (15 tests OK),
    workflow YAML parses, `go build ./...` clean.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
